  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let A and Nc denote the varieties of abelian groups and nilpotent groups of\nclass ⩽ c, respectively. Let Fr = Fr (ANc ) be a free group of rank r in ANc . An\nelement of Fr is called primitive if it can be included in a basis of Fr . Does there\nexist an algorithm recognizing primitive elements in Fr ?            E. I. Timoshenko",
